P6='<section class="sheet">\n<div class="secnum">06 &middot; REFERENCES AND RECEIPTS</div>\n<h2>References &amp; <span class="g">receipts</span></h2>\n<p class="small">All cited sources verified against primary sources as of 2026-10-17. Evidence entries are runnable artefacts in the repository, traced to tagged commits.</p>\n<div class="twocol" style="gap:30px"><div class="refgroup"><div class="refgh">Norwegian models, policy and case</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[toi1819]</span> Fl&uuml;gel et al. (2021). A forward-looking perspective on Norwegian transport models. T&Oslash;I 1819/2021.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[toi2172]</span> Tveter, E. et al. (2026). Veivalg for en realistisk og m&aring;lrettet transportplan. T&Oslash;I 2172/2026.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[tramodsim]</span> Fl&uuml;gel, Fl&ouml;tter&ouml;d, Ringdal, Weber (2023). TraModSim. T&Oslash;I 1993/2023.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[ngm]</span> Madslien, Hovi et al. Nasjonal godstransportmodell. T&Oslash;I 1247/2012; cost-model update bas&aring;r 2021 (2022).</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[hjelle]</span> Hjelle, H. M. (2010). Short Sea Shipping&rsquo;s Green Label at Risk. Transport Reviews 30(5), 617-640. DOI 10.1080/01441640903289849.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[klimalov]</span> Lov om klimam&aring;l (klimaloven), LOV-2017-06-16-60. 2050 target 90 to 95% vs 1990.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[svv25]</span> Statens vegvesen (2026). Bompengerapport 2025 (about NOK 16.8 bn; debt about NOK 78 bn, Tabell 38).</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[bypakke]</span> Bypakke Kristiansund: council 18 Apr 2024 (26-19); Storting 3 Jun 2025; tolling up to 15 yr.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[innst337]</span> Innst. 337 S (2024-2025), Prop. 87 S: Bypakke Kristiansund. Storting, 3 June 2025.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[vegamot]</span> Vegamot AS, Bypakke Kristiansund tariff: 34 / 27.20 tag / 19.04 ZE+tag; from 1 June 2026.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[snl19]</span> Bergen municipal election 2019 (valg.no/SSB): FNB 16.7%, 11 seats.</div></div><div class="refgroup"><div class="refgh">Acceptance and discrete choice</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[lepira]</span> Le Pira, Marcucci, Gatta, Inturri, Ignaccolo (2017). Integrating DCM and ABM for stakeholder policy acceptability in urban freight. Res. Transp. Econ. 64, 13-25. DOI 10.1016/j.retrec.2017.08.002</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[hybridaccept]</span> Ben-Akiva et al. (2002). Hybrid choice models. Marketing Letters 13(3), 163-175 (method anchor).</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[odeck08]</span> Odeck, Br&aring;then (2008). Travel demand elasticities and users&rsquo; attitudes: Norwegian toll projects. Transp. Res. A 42(1), 77-94.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[borjesson16]</span> B&ouml;rjesson, Eliasson, Hamilton (2016). Why experience changes attitudes to congestion pricing: Gothenburg. Transp. Res. A 85, 1-16.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[toi2179]</span> Acceptance of distance-based road pricing: national choice experiment + Oslo field trial. T&Oslash;I 2179/2026.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[iclv2]</span> Vij, Walker (2016). How, when and why integrated choice and latent variable models are latently useful. Transp. Res. B 90, 192-217. DOI 10.1016/j.trb.2016.04.021</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[marcucci17]</span> Marcucci, Le Pira, Gatta, Inturri, Ignaccolo, Pluchino (2017). Simulating participatory urban freight transport policy-making: heterogeneous stakeholder preferences and interaction effects. Transp. Res. E 103, 69-86. DOI 10.1016/j.tre.2017.04.006</div></div><div class="refgroup"><div class="refgh">ABM, pathways and robustness</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[fuhrer]</span> F&uuml;hrer, d&rsquo;Hont, Rouwette, Kwakkel (2025). Transp. Res. Interdisc. Persp. 34, 101683 [vol. to confirm]. DOI 10.1016/j.trip.2025.101683</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[haasnoot]</span> Haasnoot, Kwakkel, Walker, ter Maat (2013). Dynamic adaptive policy pathways. Glob. Environ. Change 23(2), 485-498.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[mordm]</span> Kasprzyk, Nataraj, Reed, Lempert (2013). Many-objective robust decision making. Environ. Model. Softw. 42, 55-71.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[prim]</span> Friedman, Fisher (1999). Bump hunting in high-dimensional data. Stat. Comput. 9(2), 123-143.</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[shaabani]</span> Shaabani, Hvattum, Laporte, Hoff (2024). Stability metrics for a maritime inventory routing problem. EJTL 13, 100146. DOI 10.1016/j.ejtl.2024.100146</div><div class="ref"><span class="rk">[wooldridge]</span> Wooldridge (2005). Initial conditions in dynamic nonlinear panel models. J. Appl. Econometrics 20(1), 39-54.</div></div></div>\n<div class="ledger"><div class="tcat" style="color:var(--teal)">Evidence ledger: receipts you can run</div>\n<table><tr><td class="h">[evdcm]</td><td><b>Swissmetro mixed-logit reproduction.</b> Biogeme 3.3.5, N=6,768, 1,000 Halton draws. Final LL &minus;5214.9 vs published &minus;5214.8. <span class="h">evidence/dcm-swissmetro</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td class="h">[evfid]</td><td><b>Zonal-vs-network fidelity benchmark.</b> Molde + Kristiansund OSM graphs. About 15% MAPE (r 0.73 to 0.84); MATSim dynamic cross-check 19% free-flow, breaks under 10x congestion. <span class="h">evidence/fidelity-benchmark</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td class="h">[tests]</td><td><b>89 automated tests.</b> Every figure generated from the same code; FAIR data deposit once Sikt allows. <span class="h">pytest, tagged at submission</span></td></tr></table></div>\n<div class="plate" style="margin-top:12px"><span class="plabel">The thesis as a system: data to articles to claims</span><img src="data:image/png;base64," style="">\n<div class="cap">Each data source feeds a wave; each wave feeds an article; each article delivers a claim. <span class="d">Cut the survey wires and the teal spine, my own data and national ranges, still reaches A1 and A3. The thesis completes with no outside dependency.</span></div></div>\n<div class="foot"><span>Arshad Akhtar Abbasia</span><span>References and receipts</span><span class="r">github.com/Astheno-sphere/computational_logistics &middot; 6 / 6</span></div></section>'